<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" version="2.0"><channel><title>Romans, illustrated | Romans</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/</link><description>Romans for ordinary life: three distinct teaching films in each batch.</description><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:18:21 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/feed.xml" /><item><title>What is shaping the choice I want to make?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-mind-learning-to-discern/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-a-mind-learning-to-discern-share.jpg" alt="What is shaping the choice I want to make?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12:2 connects wise decisions with a renewed mind. Scripture helps us examine desires for status or comfort and learn what pleases God.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-mind-learning-to-discern/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-mind-learning-to-discern/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-a-mind-learning-to-discern-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What can I pray when my heart won’t settle?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-prayer-for-the-restless-heart/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-a-prayer-for-the-restless-heart-share.jpg" alt="What can I pray when my heart won’t settle?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 15:13 gives a restless heart words to pray. Ask the God of hope for joy and peace as you trust him, through the Holy Spirit’s power.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 15:12–13&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-prayer-for-the-restless-heart/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-prayer-for-the-restless-heart/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-a-prayer-for-the-restless-heart-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Could an ordinary workday become gospel partnership?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-workday-becomes-partnership/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-a-workday-becomes-partnership-share.jpg" alt="Could an ordinary workday become gospel partnership?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Paul’s shared trade with Priscilla and Aquila grew into gospel partnership. Acts 18 and Romans 16 invite faithfulness to the people already near us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Acts 18:1–3; Romans 16:3–5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-workday-becomes-partnership/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/a-workday-becomes-partnership/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-a-workday-becomes-partnership-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What does adoption add to forgiveness?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/adopted-into-family/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-adopted-into-family-share.jpg" alt="What does adoption add to forgiveness?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 8 describes the Spirit of adoption and belonging as God’s children. That family hope holds through suffering on the way to glory with Christ.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 8:15–17&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/adopted-into-family/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/adopted-into-family/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-adopted-into-family-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Where does knowing God’s will begin?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/begin-with-mercy/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-begin-with-mercy-share.jpg" alt="Where does knowing God’s will begin?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12 begins discernment with God’s mercies. Offering your life to him gives a place to begin as you consider work, opportunities and people affected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:1–2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/begin-with-mercy/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/begin-with-mercy/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-begin-with-mercy-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>How can I begin when I do not know my gift?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/begin-with-service/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-begin-with-service-share.jpg" alt="How can I begin when I do not know my gift?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can begin serving before you can name your spiritual gift. Romans 12 invites practical help, wise counsel and learning alongside your church.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:3-8&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/begin-with-service/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/begin-with-service/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-begin-with-service-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Who has the final word over my guilt?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/christ-answers-the-accusation/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-christ-answers-the-accusation-share.jpg" alt="Who has the final word over my guilt?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 8 answers returning guilt with Christ’s death, resurrection and intercession. Those God has justified can rest in the Savior who speaks for them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 8:1, 33–34&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/christ-answers-the-accusation/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/christ-answers-the-accusation/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-christ-answers-the-accusation-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Who could encourage an apostle?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/even-paul-received-encouragement/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-even-paul-received-encouragement-share.jpg" alt="Who could encourage an apostle?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In Romans 1, Paul expects ordinary believers to encourage his faith too. Christian service includes receiving strength as well as offering it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 1:11–12&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/even-paul-received-encouragement/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/even-paul-received-encouragement/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-even-paul-received-encouragement-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Can I choose faithfully while I still feel uncertain?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/faithful-without-perfect-certainty/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-faithful-without-perfect-certainty-share.jpg" alt="Can I choose faithfully while I still feel uncertain?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12 invites thoughtful discernment as God renews our minds. Scripture, prayer and wise counsel can guide a faithful step amid uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/faithful-without-perfect-certainty/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/faithful-without-perfect-certainty/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-faithful-without-perfect-certainty-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>How do I fight sin without relying on myself?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/fight-sin-by-the-spirit/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-fight-sin-by-the-spirit-share.jpg" alt="How do I fight sin without relying on myself?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 8 calls believers to put sinful deeds to death by the Spirit. Bring ordinary temptations to God and depend on his help as you turn from sin.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 8:9–15&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/fight-sin-by-the-spirit/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/fight-sin-by-the-spirit/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-fight-sin-by-the-spirit-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Can God forgive the sin I still remember?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/forgiven-even-when-you-remember/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-forgiven-even-when-you-remember-share.jpg" alt="Can God forgive the sin I still remember?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 4 speaks of real forgiveness for real guilt. A painful memory can be brought honestly to God while faith rests in his mercy through Christ.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 4:5–8&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/forgiven-even-when-you-remember/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/forgiven-even-when-you-remember/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-forgiven-even-when-you-remember-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What matters more than winning a food argument?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/freedom-guided-by-love/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-freedom-guided-by-love-share.jpg" alt="What matters more than winning a food argument?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 14 asks how our choices affect another believer’s conscience. Love pursues peace and builds up the person for whom Christ died.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 14:1–4, 15–19&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/freedom-guided-by-love/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/freedom-guided-by-love/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-freedom-guided-by-love-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why would I help someone who hurt me?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/goodness-that-does-not-keep-score/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-goodness-that-does-not-keep-score-share.jpg" alt="Why would I help someone who hurt me?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12 calls us to meet an enemy’s real need. Christ’s mercy can shape a wise act of kindness without buying an apology or pretending trust is restored.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:20–21; 5:8–10&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/goodness-that-does-not-keep-score/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/goodness-that-does-not-keep-score/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-goodness-that-does-not-keep-score-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why did Paul want to preach the gospel to Christians?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/gospel-for-believers/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-gospel-for-believers-share.jpg" alt="Why did Paul want to preach the gospel to Christians?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Paul wanted to preach the gospel to believers in Rome. Romans 1 shows why familiar good news about Christ continues to nourish and deepen Christian faith.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 1:8, 15–17&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/gospel-for-believers/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/gospel-for-believers/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-gospel-for-believers-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why do I feel less gifted than everyone else?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/grace-before-comparison/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-grace-before-comparison-share.jpg" alt="Why do I feel less gifted than everyone else?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12:3–8 helps us receive our different gifts with humility. God’s grace gives you a place to serve without becoming the person beside you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:3-8&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/grace-before-comparison/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/grace-before-comparison/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-grace-before-comparison-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why does Paul call grace a gift?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/grace-is-a-gift/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-grace-is-a-gift-share.jpg" alt="Why does Paul call grace a gift?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 3–4 contrasts earned wages with God’s gift of righteousness. Faith receives what Christ has secured, leaving us grateful and without grounds to boast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 3:24–28; 4:4–5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/grace-is-a-gift/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/grace-is-a-gift/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-grace-is-a-gift-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Does Christian hope mean I should stop crying?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/hope-can-make-room-for-tears/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-hope-can-make-room-for-tears-share.jpg" alt="Does Christian hope mean I should stop crying?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 8 gives grieving believers resurrection hope while acknowledging their groaning. Romans 12 calls us to share their tears and remain beside them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 8:23–25; 12:15&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/hope-can-make-room-for-tears/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/hope-can-make-room-for-tears/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-hope-can-make-room-for-tears-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>If I give up revenge, does the wrong still matter?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/justice-without-personal-revenge/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-justice-without-personal-revenge-share.jpg" alt="If I give up revenge, does the wrong still matter?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12–13 distinguishes personal revenge from proper accountability. You can seek protection and tell the truth while entrusting final judgment to God.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:18–19; 13:3–4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/justice-without-personal-revenge/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/justice-without-personal-revenge/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-justice-without-personal-revenge-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why do I know better, yet still sin?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/knowing-the-rule-cannot-rescue/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-knowing-the-rule-cannot-rescue-share.jpg" alt="Why do I know better, yet still sin?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 7 shows how God’s good law exposes sin without supplying its cure. Romans 8 directs our hope for rescue to what God has done through Christ.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 7:7–25; 8:1–4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/knowing-the-rule-cannot-rescue/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/knowing-the-rule-cannot-rescue/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-knowing-the-rule-cannot-rescue-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>How can I help after the first visit?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/love-after-the-first-visit/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-love-after-the-first-visit-share.jpg" alt="How can I help after the first visit?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Shared sorrow continues through prayer and practical care. Romans 12 encourages specific offers of help and patient attention after the first visit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:9,12–13,15&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/love-after-the-first-visit/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/love-after-the-first-visit/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-love-after-the-first-visit-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>How far does God’s love reach?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/love-that-reaches-the-nations/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-love-that-reaches-the-nations-share.jpg" alt="How far does God’s love reach?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans connects God’s mercy with the gospel reaching the nations. Prayer, giving and shared sending let a local church take part in that purpose.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 1:5–7; 15:8–12,20–24; 16:25–27&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/love-that-reaches-the-nations/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/love-that-reaches-the-nations/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-love-that-reaches-the-nations-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>How do I know God loves me when life hurts?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/loved-and-brought-near/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-loved-and-brought-near-share.jpg" alt="How do I know God loves me when life hurts?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Christ’s death shows God’s love for sinners, and suffering cannot separate his people from that love. Romans 5 and 8 invite hurting hearts to draw near.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 5:6–11; 8:35–39&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/loved-and-brought-near/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/loved-and-brought-near/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-loved-and-brought-near-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why does God’s love bring us together?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/loved-into-a-shared-life/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-loved-into-a-shared-life-share.jpg" alt="Why does God’s love bring us together?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12 and 15 describe life together in Christ: receiving help, strengthening others and welcoming people with the patience his mercy has shown us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:4–5; 15:1–7&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/loved-into-a-shared-life/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/loved-into-a-shared-life/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-loved-into-a-shared-life-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Do I have to say yes to every need?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/members-of-one-another/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-members-of-one-another-share.jpg" alt="Do I have to say yes to every need?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12 pictures a body whose members have different gifts. Share the work, receive help and serve faithfully without trying to meet every need yourself.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:3-8&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/members-of-one-another/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/members-of-one-another/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-members-of-one-another-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What about the harm I have caused?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/mercy-gives-courage-to-make-amends/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-mercy-gives-courage-to-make-amends-share.jpg" alt="What about the harm I have caused?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;God’s mercy gives courage to admit harm, listen and change. Romans 12 calls us to pursue peace while respecting another person’s time and boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:9, 17–18; 13:8–10&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/mercy-gives-courage-to-make-amends/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/mercy-gives-courage-to-make-amends/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-mercy-gives-courage-to-make-amends-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why Romans ends with names</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/names-matter/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-names-matter-share.jpg" alt="Why Romans ends with names" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Phoebe, Priscilla, Aquila and Mary help us see the people living out the gospel in Romans 16. Their greetings invite gratitude for faithful people nearby.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 16:1–13&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/names-matter/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/names-matter/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-names-matter-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What is God’s patience inviting us to do?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/patience-and-repentance/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-patience-and-repentance-share.jpg" alt="What is God’s patience inviting us to do?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 2:4 warns against taking God’s kindness for granted. His patience invites us to name the sin we excuse and turn to him for mercy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 2:4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/patience-and-repentance/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/patience-and-repentance/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-patience-and-repentance-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Can I have peace with God on an anxious day?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/peace-on-an-anxious-day/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-peace-on-an-anxious-day-share.jpg" alt="Can I have peace with God on an anxious day?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 5:1–2 grounds peace with God in what Christ has secured. You can bring him an anxious mind while standing in the grace he has given you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 5:1–2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/peace-on-an-anxious-day/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/peace-on-an-anxious-day/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-peace-on-an-anxious-day-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>If I am free, why am I still tempted?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/sin-is-not-your-master/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-sin-is-not-your-master-share.jpg" alt="If I am free, why am I still tempted?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 6 distinguishes temptation’s presence from sin’s mastery. Those united to Christ can remember their new life and offer their words and actions to God.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 6:1–14&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/sin-is-not-your-master/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/sin-is-not-your-master/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-sin-is-not-your-master-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What can a quiet conversation do?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-conversation-beside-the-crowd/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-the-conversation-beside-the-crowd-share.jpg" alt="What can a quiet conversation do?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Priscilla and Aquila helped Apollos understand God’s way more accurately. Their patient conversation invites us to open Scripture with someone who needs help.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Acts 18:24–28; Romans 16:3&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-conversation-beside-the-crowd/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-conversation-beside-the-crowd/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-the-conversation-beside-the-crowd-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Does evil get the last word?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-god-of-peace-and-the-last-word/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-the-god-of-peace-and-the-last-word-share.jpg" alt="Does evil get the last word?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 16 promises that the God of peace will defeat Satan. A troubled church can hold to the gospel and choose what is good while evil still threatens.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 16:17–20&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-god-of-peace-and-the-last-word/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-god-of-peace-and-the-last-word/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-the-god-of-peace-and-the-last-word-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What should a grafted branch remember?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-root-supports-you/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-the-root-supports-you-share.jpg" alt="What should a grafted branch remember?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 11 pictures Gentile believers as grafted olive branches. Dependence on God’s mercy calls for gratitude and humility toward Jewish people.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 11:17–22&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-root-supports-you/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/the-root-supports-you/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-the-root-supports-you-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What does “good” mean?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/what-good-means/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-what-good-means-share.jpg" alt="What does “good” mean?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 8:28–30 connects God’s promise of good with becoming like Christ. Read the promise beside its purpose when suffering makes the future hard to see.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 8:28–30&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/what-good-means/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/what-good-means/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-what-good-means-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>Why does getting even leave me worse off?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/when-payback-keeps-evil-moving/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-when-payback-keeps-evil-moving-share.jpg" alt="Why does getting even leave me worse off?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A cruel reply can carry someone else’s hurt further. Romans 12 calls us to truthful words shaped by mercy and to overcome evil with good.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:17–18,21&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/when-payback-keeps-evil-moving/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/when-payback-keeps-evil-moving/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-when-payback-keeps-evil-moving-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>What if I don’t know what to say to someone grieving?</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/when-you-have-no-words/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-when-you-have-no-words-share.jpg" alt="What if I don’t know what to say to someone grieving?" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 12:15 invites us to stay beside people who grieve. Listening, shared silence and patient company can express love when an explanation cannot help.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 12:9–10,15&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/when-you-have-no-words/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/when-you-have-no-words/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-when-you-have-no-words-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item><item><title>When words fail</title><link>https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/words-fail/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-words-fail-share.jpg" alt="When words fail" width="1200" height="630"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans 8:26–27 speaks to weakness in prayer: the Spirit intercedes according to God’s will. Bring God the words you have, even when they feel unfinished.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Romans, illustrated · Romans 8:26–27&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/words-fail/"&gt;Watch the film and read the narration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><category>Romans, illustrated</category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://romansbook.com/series/romans-illustrated/words-fail/</guid><media:thumbnail url="https://romansbook.com/assets/covers/shorts-words-fail-share.jpg" width="1200" height="630" /></item></channel></rss>